This product includes software developed by Ioannis Kalogeris (NTUA).

Portions of this software were implemented following algorithms published in:

  Liu, Wang & Li, "CK-MPM: A Compact-Kernel Material Point Method",
  ACM Transactions on Graphics 44(4), 2025. The reference implementation is
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  See src/scion/materials/hencky.py and src/scion/materials/fluid.py.

  O'Hare, Gourgiotis, Coombs & Augarde, "An implicit Material Point Method for
  micropolar solids undergoing large deformations", Computer Methods in Applied
  Mechanics and Engineering 419 (2024) 116668, published under CC BY.
  See src/scion/discretization/mpm/implicit.py and
  src/scion/discretization/mpm/micropolar.py.

The underlying constitutive models predate both references and are cited
individually in the docstring of each class.
